title: The SLD apparatus route

# Stage 4 owns the legal and constitutional entry contract. This route keeps
# that party, its seats, assets and filed lists in the shared simulation while
# letting the apparatus settle its rivals and choose what it is for.

@sld_congress
# prose-audit: Grade A — The route names the legal vehicle, inherited assets,
# regional secretaries and rival currents, then makes consolidation an explicit
# choice rather than treating generic baron strength as an authored victory.
title: The SLD apparatus decides whether it is the party
subtitle: A legal vehicle, a regional machine and control of nominations can become an ascendancy
face-image: img/poland/events/left-congress.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 28
order: 4
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and sld_partocracy_available = 1 and ((year = 2023 and month >= 8) or year = 2024 or year = 2025 or year = 2026)
on-arrival: {!
const originLabels = {
    centralized_executive: "the centralised SLD executive written into the merger statute",
    asset_led_executive: "the temporary executive that first secured the leases, accounts and legal shell",
    machine_counter_coup: "the registration counter-coup that displaced the merger's political leadership",
    baron_ascendancy: "the baron ascendancy ratified inside the common party",
    miller_restoration: "Miller's old-left restoration and its locked command of the leadership office"
};
Q.sld_partocracy_origin_label = originLabels[Q.sld_partocracy_origin] ||
    "the surviving SLD apparatus";
Q.sld_partocracy_rival_label = [
    Q.spring_active && Q.spring_in_left ? "Wiosna" : "",
    Q.progressives_active && Q.progressives_in_left
        ? String(Q.progressives_name || "the progressive current") : "",
    Q.razem_active ? "Razem" : "",
    Q.pps_active && Q.pps_in_left ? "PPS" : "",
    Q.social_patriot_active && Q.social_patriot_in_left
        ? String(Q.social_patriot_name || "the social-patriot current") : "",
    Q.labor_active && Q.labor_in_left
        ? String(Q.labor_name || "the labour-first current") : ""
].filter(Boolean).join(", ") || "no organised challenger";
Q.news_headline = "The SLD executive calls a congress about ownership of the party";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — The people who hold the keys

The opening report does not call this a leadership contest. It lists the
registry entry, the leases, the campaign account, the county offices and the
regional secretaries authorised to submit candidates. Together they amount to
**[+ sld_partocracy_origin_label +]**.

That is enough to run a party and not enough to settle what the party is.
**[+ sld_partocracy_rival_label +]** still has MPs, organisers or an outside
legal identity. The apparatus can remain the strongest current in a generic
Lewica settlement, or it can say plainly that SLD owns the organisation and
every other current must bargain with it from that fact.

- @sld_claim
- @sld_decline

@sld_claim
