go-to: sld_rivals

@sld_decline
title: Keep baron dominance inside the existing settlement
subtitle: The machine remains strong without claiming a distinct SLD route
on-arrival: sld_partocracy_declined = 1; party_unity += 2; barons_dissent -= 3; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The apparatus chooses influence without an SLD restoration"

The executive keeps its offices, nominations and bargaining weight, but does
not turn them into a claim that SLD is the whole party. Baron strength remains
real and playable through the ordinary caucus system; no democratic renewal is
required to make that choice useful.

- @poland_event_queue: Keep the existing settlement

@sld_rivals
# prose-audit: Grade A — Every settlement says whether Wiosna, Razem,
# Wspólne Jutro/progressives and smaller challengers submit, survive under
# administrative exclusion, or send a named organisation through the existing
# party-and-seat exit machinery.
title: The apparatus writes the terms for every rival current
subtitle: Co-option, marginalisation and expulsion preserve different things
new-page: true

= The nominations meeting

The SLD victory is organisational. It still has to be translated into people:
who receives a bureau desk, who keeps access to membership records, who signs
the common list and who is told to register elsewhere.

Co-option keeps activists and parliamentary breadth, but spends money and
makes the victory less complete. Administrative marginalisation keeps every
seat in place while closing nominations and programme authority. Expulsion is
cleanest only on the organisational chart: the existing caucus resolver will
move MPs, legal identity, polling and committee status rather than deleting
them.

- @rivals_coopt
- @rivals_marginalize
- @expel_spring
- @expel_progressives
- @expel_razem
- @expel_pps
- @expel_social_patriot
- @expel_labor

@rivals_coopt
title: Buy submission with bureau posts and protected list places
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Rivals submit; breadth and activists survive, while patronage and coalition suspicion rise
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Co-option needs two resources worth of staff, travel and protected campaign places.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.sld_partocracy_stage = 2;
Q.sld_partocracy_rival_settlement = "coopted";
Q.sld_partocracy_started_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
for (const rival of ["spring", "progressives", "razem", "pps", "social_patriot", "labor"]) {
    if (!Q[rival + "_active"]) continue;
    Q[rival + "_org_status"] = Q[rival + "_in_left"]
        ? "subordinate_current" : "subordinate_electoral_partner";
    Q[rival + "_dissent"] -= 8;
    Q[rival + "_demand_answered"] = 1;
    Q[rival + "_escalation_stage"] = 0;
}
Q.barons_strength += 2;
Q.party_unity += 6;
Q.internal_dissent -= 4;
Q.organiser_energy += 2;
Q.list_confidence += 3;
Q.sld_patronage_exposure += 5;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += Q.left_in_government ? 2 : 0;
Q.public_trust -= 2;
Q.news_headline = "SLD buys submission without breaking the parliamentary family";
!}

Nobody is asked to pretend that they won. Wiosna and the progressive network
keep named posts; Razem keeps written list places or its partner status; smaller
currents retain a room and a budget line. In return, the SLD executive signs
the lists and can dismiss the staff. The coalition remains broad, expensive and
obviously managed through appointments.

- @poland_event_queue: File the patronage compact

@rivals_marginalize
title: Close nominations and leave the currents alive at the edge
subtitle: Rivals survive but lose programme and list control; discipline rises as activists and trust fall
on-arrival: {!
Q.sld_partocracy_stage = 2;
Q.sld_partocracy_rival_settlement = "marginalized";
Q.sld_partocracy_started_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
for (const rival of ["spring", "progressives", "razem", "pps", "social_patriot", "labor"]) {
    if (!Q[rival + "_active"]) continue;
    Q[rival + "_org_status"] = Q[rival + "_in_left"]
        ? "marginalized_current" : "marginalized_electoral_partner";
    Q[rival + "_dissent"] += 8;
    Q[rival + "_grievance_memory"] += 5;
}
Q.barons_strength += 5;
Q.local_network += 3;
Q.list_confidence += 6;
Q.leadership_authority += 3;
Q.party_unity += 1;
Q.organiser_energy -= 5;
Q.young_support -= 2;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 2;
Q.public_trust -= 2;
Q.news_headline = "The SLD executive closes nominations without dissolving its rivals";
!}

The currents remain legal and visible. Their MPs retain their seats and their
members retain their names. What they lose is the practical ability to turn a
motion into a candidate, a candidate into a list place, or a programme demand
into a deadline. The apparatus gains order and starts losing the people who
used to make an election look like a cause.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the closed list rules

