@rivals_expel_commit
title: The expulsion letters are served
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const target = String(Q.caucus_exit_target || "");
Q.sld_partocracy_stage = 2;
Q.sld_partocracy_rival_settlement = "expelled_" + target;
Q.sld_partocracy_started_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
for (const rival of ["spring", "progressives", "razem", "pps", "social_patriot", "labor"]) {
    if (!Q[rival + "_active"]) continue;
    Q[rival + "_org_status"] = rival == target
        ? "expelled_party"
        : (Q[rival + "_in_left"]
            ? "marginalized_current" : "marginalized_electoral_partner");
}
Q.caucus_exit_mode = "punitive";
Q.barons_strength += 4;
Q.list_confidence += 5;
Q.leadership_authority += 4;
Q.sld_patronage_exposure += 2;
Q.news_headline = "SLD expels one rival and marginalizes the rest";
!}
go-to: poland_caucus_dynamics.resolve_exit

@sld_doctrine
# prose-audit: Grade A — Each doctrine names an electorate, an organisational
# advantage and the constituency or institution that pays for it.
title: SLD decides what the machine is for
subtitle: Tradition, competent accommodation with business, or organisation without renewal
face-image: img/poland/events/wlodzimierz-czarzasty-2019.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 28
order: 5
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and sld_partocracy_stage = 2 and sld_partocracy_doctrine = "none" and time >= sld_partocracy_started_time + 1

= [+ date_label +] — Three doctrines for one apparatus

The party can now nominate candidates and survive a bad month. That is an
achievement, not a programme. Three drafts reach the executive.

The orthodox draft treats SLD as institutional memory: traditional social
democracy, pensions, secular government and continuity. The market draft
treats the same memory as administrative competence: mayors, specialists and a
business-friendly economic line. The third draft avoids renewal altogether.
It says that voters change and programmes expire, while incumbency, assets,
discipline and local networks remain.

- @doctrine_orthodox
- @doctrine_market
- @doctrine_partocracy

@doctrine_orthodox
title: Orthodox SLD — pensions, secularism and institutional continuity
subtitle: Older and public-service voters gain a clear home; activist energy and generational renewal pay the bill
on-arrival: {!
Q.sld_partocracy_stage = 3;
Q.sld_partocracy_doctrine = "orthodox";
Q.sld_partocracy_doctrine_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.left_economic_position -= 5;
Q.left_right_score -= 3;
Q.left_cultural_position -= 3;
Q.pensioner_support += 7;
Q.public_sector_support += 4;
Q.workers_support += 2;
Q.public_mood_pending_secular_state_left_ownership += 6;
Q.institutional_trust += 3;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 2;
Q.barons_strength += 3;
Q.party_unity += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 4;
Q.organiser_energy -= 4;
Q.young_support -= 4;
Q.media_capacity -= 1;
Q.news_headline = "SLD adopts an orthodox social-democratic and secular doctrine";
!}

The programme restores a recognisable promise: indexed pensions, durable
public services, a secular state and institutions repaired rather than
reinvented at every congress. Older households and public employees know what
the initials stand for again. The stage contains very few people who joined
politics in the last decade, and the volunteer desk notices before television
does.

- @poland_event_queue: Adopt the orthodox programme

@doctrine_market
title: Market apparatus — business confidence and competent local government
subtitle: Money, mayors and administrative delivery improve; labour trust and the left flank retreat
on-arrival: {!
Q.sld_partocracy_stage = 3;
Q.sld_partocracy_doctrine = "market_apparatus";
Q.sld_partocracy_doctrine_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.left_economic_position += 7;
Q.left_right_score += 5;
Q.resources += 3;
Q.local_network += 4;
Q.administrative_capacity += 5;
Q.government_delivery += 3;
Q.market_liberal_support += 7;
Q.liberal_professionals_left_affinity += 3;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.p2050_relation += 3;
Q.barons_strength += 2;
Q.labor_dissent += 10;
Q.union_trust -= 7;
Q.opzz_cooperation -= 5;
Q.razem_dissent += 8;
Q.workers_support -= 3;
Q.public_sector_support -= 2;
Q.party_unity -= 2;
Q.news_headline = "SLD presents its mayors and managers as a market-friendly governing class";
!}

The party stops apologising for the people in it who have balanced municipal
budgets, negotiated investment and administered services. Business donors and
professionals and academics see a Left they can imagine in an economy ministry. The
unions see experienced officials explaining why the affordable programme is
always the one employers already prefer.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the competence programme

@doctrine_partocracy
title: Reform-avoidant partocracy — assets, discipline and incumbency first
subtitle: The strongest lists and local machine; corruption exposure, weak enthusiasm and coalition distrust accumulate
on-arrival: {!
Q.sld_partocracy_stage = 3;
Q.sld_partocracy_doctrine = "partocracy";
Q.sld_partocracy_doctrine_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.resources += 2;
Q.local_network += 7;
Q.barons_strength += 7;
Q.list_confidence += 8;
Q.leadership_authority += 5;
Q.turnout_readiness += 3;
Q.party_unity += 4;
Q.sld_patronage_exposure += 12;
Q.public_trust -= 5;
Q.organiser_energy -= 6;
Q.young_support -= 5;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 4;
Q.ko_relation -= 4;
Q.psl_relation -= 3;
Q.p2050_relation -= 3;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += Q.left_in_government ? 4 : 0;
Q.news_headline = "SLD chooses incumbency and organisation over ideological renewal";
!}

No manifesto clause outranks the rule that the party must still exist after a
bad election. Regional chairs select candidates early, officeholders fund the
campaign and every list has a whip before it has a slogan. It is formidable in
county halls and lifeless in volunteer meetings. Coalition partners know that
an SLD promise may be a policy commitment or a price for the next appointment,
and budget accordingly.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the apparatus back to work

@sld_election_endpoint
# prose-audit: Grade A — The endpoint converts accumulated organisation and
# accumulated costs into votes or bargaining leverage, without erasing
# breakaway parties or inventing a second election model.
title: The SLD machine reaches the election
subtitle: Cash the organisation in for turnout, or reserve it for safe places and coalition leverage
face-image: img/poland/events/election-2023-ballot.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 30
order: 3
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2027 and month = 8 and sld_partocracy_stage = 3 and sld_election_endpoint_done = 0
on-arrival: {!
const organisation =
    (Number(Q.barons_strength) || 0) * 0.08 +
    (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) * 0.05 +
    (Number(Q.list_confidence) || 0) * 0.05 +
    Math.min(10, Math.max(0, Number(Q.resources) || 0)) * 0.15;
const costs =
    (Number(Q.sld_patronage_exposure) || 0) * 0.05 +
    Math.max(0, 50 - (Number(Q.organiser_energy) || 0)) * 0.04 +
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 25) * 0.03;
const doctrineBonus = Q.sld_partocracy_doctrine == "orthodox"
    ? (Number(Q.pensioner_support) || 0) * 0.015
    : (Q.sld_partocracy_doctrine == "market_apparatus"
        ? (Number(Q.administrative_capacity) || 0) * 0.04
        : (Number(Q.barons_strength) || 0) * 0.025);
Q.sld_election_payoff = Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(6, Math.round((organisation + doctrineBonus - costs - 6) * 10) / 10)
);
Q.sld_election_payoff_label = Q.sld_election_payoff >= 3
    ? "A formidable election machine"
    : (Q.sld_election_payoff >= 0
        ? "A stable but low-enthusiasm machine"
        : "An apparatus whose costs now exceed its reach");
Q.news_headline = "SLD counts offices, lists and liabilities before the election";
!}

= August 2027 — [+ sld_election_payoff_label +]

The electoral ledger is not a morality play. The organisation built by the
route is worth **[+ sld_election_payoff +] points of deployable payoff** after
patronage exposure, lost organisers and coalition friction are charged against
it.

[? if sld_partocracy_doctrine = "orthodox": The pension and secular-state
programme supplies a loyal electorate, while an ageing platform supplies fewer
new messengers.?][? if sld_partocracy_doctrine = "market_apparatus": Mayors,
managers and donors supply competence and money, while labour organisers no
longer supply it for free.?][? if sld_partocracy_doctrine = "partocracy": The
list is the best organised of the three and the least capable of explaining
why anyone without an office should care.?]

- @endpoint_turnout
- @endpoint_leverage

@endpoint_turnout
title: Spend the machine on turnout and the SLD list
subtitle: Convert the net payoff into polling momentum and election-day readiness
on-arrival: {!
Q.sld_election_endpoint_done = 1;
Q.left_poll_momentum += Number(Q.sld_election_payoff) * 0.16;
Q.turnout_readiness += Math.max(0, Number(Q.sld_election_payoff)) * 1.5;
Q.resources = Math.max(0, Number(Q.resources) - 1);
Q.sld_patronage_exposure += Q.sld_partocracy_doctrine == "partocracy" ? 3 : 1;
Q.news_headline = "SLD deploys every regional office behind its own list";
!}

Regional chairs receive turnout targets, transport budgets and the final list
of members who have not yet voted. A strong organisation converts into votes;
a tired or exposed one merely broadcasts its weakness more efficiently.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the election campaign

@endpoint_leverage
title: Protect the safe places and bargain with the likely coalition
subtitle: Less national enthusiasm, more list discipline and post-election leverage
on-arrival: {!
Q.sld_election_endpoint_done = 1;
Q.negotiation_capital += Math.max(1, Number(Q.sld_election_payoff) * 0.7);
Q.list_confidence += 4;
Q.party_unity += 2;
Q.left_poll_momentum += Math.min(0.2, Number(Q.sld_election_payoff) * 0.05);
Q.turnout_readiness -= 2;
Q.ko_relation -= Q.sld_partocracy_doctrine == "market_apparatus" ? 0 : 2;
Q.news_headline = "SLD reserves its strongest organisation for lists and coalition bargaining";
!}

The apparatus protects incumbents, district organisers and the people who will
sit across from a coalition partner after the count. It forgoes some reach in
exchange for a parliamentary delegation that knows exactly whom it owes.

- @poland_event_queue: Take the protected list into the campaign
